<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- SYNTHETIC fixture. Not RIS content.

     Exercises the P2 containment-attachment mechanism for the four
     non-'kompetenz' anwendungsbereiche_bindung values, against the combined
     single-heading grammar used by SEK1.D/E and all three primary subjects
     (unlike sek1_mathematik_mini.xml, which is SEK1.M's own two-section
     shape). Each subject below is parsed with its own throwaway SubjectSpec
     in test_parse_lehrplan.py, these are not shipped specs.

       BEREICHFACH  bindung='bereich': one AB block per area, and (mirroring
                    SEK1.D's 'Integrativer Kompetenzbereich Sprachbewusstsein
                    und Sprachreflexion') a second area with an AB block but
                    no competence list of its own.
       STUFEFACH    bindung='stufe': one AB block per school year, after
                    the last area, attached to the stufe only (never to
                    Beta, the last area seen).
       PROSAFACH    bindung='prosa': 'Anwendungsbereiche' followed by prose,
                    no liste: zero items, section existence only logged.
       KEINEFACH    bindung='keine': no Anwendungsbereiche marker at all.
       LPZFACH      bindung='bereich': ends via the LEHRPLANZUSATZ
                    belt-and-braces terminator (no legend table), proving
                    the content after it is never reached, let alone
                    double-counted under a colliding area name.

     BEREICHFACH, STUFEFACH and PROSAFACH each end with the per-subject
     footnote legend table (the general terminator); KEINEFACH does too, to
     confirm the terminator does not depend on an AB block ever having
     existed. LPZFACH instead relies solely on the second terminator.
-->
